      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GIRT BY SEA (10) couldn't have hoped to find a better race for the second start than what she finds here. Beat home all bar a talented type on debut, so will have taken benefit from that and clearly looks the one to beat. FRAM STRAIT (1) finished 2.75 lengths from the winner in fourth last start over 1400m at Pakenham Synthetic, an improvement on his seventh at Morphettville Parks the run before. Has some performances on the board that would be good enough to give this a shake. INTERVENED (3) resumes after six months and looks forward enough following a Ballarat trial win. Will find this much easier and is one to consider. WELKIN STAR (9) finished sixth two runs back then improved last start but found a couple better over 1600m at Bairnsdale, beaten 5.5 lengths. Big chance to feature in the top three provided he gets the right run from the wide gate. LAST SUMMER (5) has had a heap of chances, but not many in races of this quality, so might be one for exotics.",
